// EXPECT: chain ok 200
// EXPECT: done

// Deep `else if` chains (200 links here) used to overflow the stack in the
// PARSE phase: the else slot re-entered the full expression grammar per link
// (~18 native frames per clause in both compilers, plus the formatter's
// parser), so ~150 links crashed with a stack overflow. The parser now
// consumes `else if` iteratively (same nested AST shape; sema already
// flattened chains iteratively).
//
// Negative control: reverting the iterative parse blows the stack around 150
// links -- the process dies on a signal and the case goes red.

let classify(n: Int): String = {
